    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, i get that some people try to do both, but doesn't the shift toward \"art as activism\" inherently devalue the art itself? like, if a piece only exists to deliver a political sermon, it's basically just propaganda, right? even if it's well-crafted, it loses that universal quality that great art used to have.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
