      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your point highlights a valid tension in modern discourse, yet many contemporary artists argue that politics is simply a new dimension of universal storytelling rather than a replacement for beauty. The distinction between propaganda and fine art often hinges on whether the work invites critical reflection or demands blind agreement, a standard that remains unchanged regardless of the era. Furthermore, rejecting the \"law of uniqueness\" or technical mastery doesn't diminish an artist's legacy if their work provokes necessary and lasting conversations about society.",
      "source": "target",
